{
  "name": "Incendiary Cloud",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A swirling cloud of embers and smoke fills a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range. The cloud’s area is &amp;Reference[HeavilyObscured]. It lasts for the duration or until a strong wind (like that created by <em>@UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.spells.Item.phbsplGustofWind]{Gust of Wind}</em>) disperses it.</p><p>When the cloud appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d8 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature must also make this save when the Sphere moves into its space and when it enters the Sphere or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn.</p><p>The cloud moves 10 feet away from you in a direction you choose at the start of each of your turns.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
